  "h1": "HSA vs HRA: Ownership, Rules, and Key Differences",
  "introText": "An HSA is an account you own and fund, while an HRA is an employer-funded reimbursement arrangement you cannot fund yourself. At The Modern Wallet, we evaluate healthcare accounts through direct tax guidelines and practical financial planning. Deciding how to handle an HSA vs HRA comes down to who controls the balance and which health insurance policy covers you. An HSA requires enrollment in a qualifying high deductible health plan, allows personal contributions, and stays with you when you leave your job. An HRA is established entirely by an employer, relies solely on company money, and may end when your employment terminates. Because an HSA belongs to you, it provides long-term portability that an employer arrangement cannot offer.",
